#: ../../upstream/docs/user/server-side-search/index.rst:81
msgid "Search as you type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/server-side-search/index.rst:83
msgid ""
"Search as-you-type allows users to quickly find exactly what they are "
"looking for while typing. It also saves recent searches, for future "
"reference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/server-side-search/index.rst:86
msgid "Try it by pressing :guilabel:`/` (forward slash) and typing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/server-side-search/index.rst:89
msgid "Configuring search"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/server-side-search/index.rst:91
msgid ""
"You can configure search options for your project from the "
":term:`dashboard`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/server-side-search/index.rst:93
msgid ""
"Go to your project's :menuselection:`Settings --> Search`. From there you"
" can toggle :guilabel:`Enable search modal`, which controls whether the "
"Read the Docs search modal is shown in your documentation, and "
":guilabel:`Show subprojects filter in search modal`, which controls "
"whether readers can filter search results by :doc:`subproject "
"</subprojects>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/server-side-search/index.rst:100
msgid "How main content is detected"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/server-side-search/index.rst:102
msgid ""
"Server Side Search indexes the \"main content\" of HTML pages, ignoring "
"headers, footers, navigation, and other page elements that aren't part of"
" the documentation content itself. This keeps results focused and avoids "
"repeated elements like nav menus from polluting relevance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/server-side-search/index.rst:106
msgid ""
"For details on how the main content area is detected, see :ref:`reference"
"/main-content-detection:detection logic`."
msgstr ""

